; Zen gather/scatter costs under a mask that is known at compile time.
;
; A legalized part with no active lane has nothing to gather, so CodeGen folds
; it away: a v24i32 operation indexed by qwords splits into three eight-lane
; parts, but a mask holding only eight live lanes leaves one instruction. The
; cost must follow the parts that survive, not the parts the shape implies, or
; a partially masked operation is charged several times over.
;
; The premium follows the live lanes for the same reason -- a lane that is
; masked off has no scalar load to be measured against -- so a gather whose
; live lanes fill one eight-lane part costs what the v8i32 gather it compiles
; to costs. The reference functions below pin that equality.
;
; The scatter does not reach it, and the reference pins the gap rather than the
; equality: a v16i32 scatter clears its body by 5 where a v4i32 one clears it
; by 11, so the margin a scatter is measured against does not grow with the
; row. Pricing the live lanes against the row that fits them would then charge
; a partly masked scatter more than the same scatter fully live, for the one
; instruction both emit, so the narrowest margin among the rows that could
; describe the operation is the one charged. That holds the scatter below its
; v8i32 reference instead of level with it. The rows are the reason -- the
; v16i32 and v16f32 scatter totals are low against their own v4 and v8
; neighbours -- and correcting them is a recalibration with its own
; measurements, not a change to the accounting here.

; RUN: opt < %s -S -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -passes="print<cost-model>" 2>&1 -disable-output -cost-kind=throughput -mcpu=znver4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RTHRU
; RUN: opt < %s -S -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -passes="print<cost-model>" 2>&1 -disable-output -cost-kind=code-size -mcpu=znver4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CODESIZE

